				<string>Four legs, each logging before the next runs, because the failure being chased is one that kills the run. Probe-InlineBench came back as a single empty line and could not say whether the coercion refused a data: URL, ran no script, or timed out on the network. a: static HTML, no script. b: a script that rewrites its own line. c: a real https URL. d: sync and async requests from the page. Read the first empty line: everything above it worked. The two controls are inline rather than $file because a two-line payload is not worth a page, which is also what js-data-url does.</string>
